<p>Today I merged the full redesign of the site. A few things I’m happy with:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Warm-botanical palette</strong> — soft white (<code>#FDF6ED</code>) with a muted green (<code>#778873</code>) and warm brown. Reads “researcher” without feeling corporate.</li>
<li><strong>DAG motifs</strong> — a faint animated directed-acyclic-graph behind the hero, and my career rendered as an actual DAG on the About page. On-theme for causal inference work.</li>
<li><strong>LLM-friendly layer</strong> — a curated <code>llms.txt</code>, clean Markdown mirrors of every page, and schema.org JSON-LD (Article, Person, ProfilePage, VideoObject) via a small Lua filter. Google ignores <code>llms.txt</code> but uses the structured data, so I did both.</li>
<li><strong>Talks carousel</strong> — a single-card infinite carousel for the talk recordings, with a lightbox player.</li>
</ul>
<p>The build is a Quarto project deployed to GitHub Pages from the committed <code>docs/</code> folder. The whole thing renders from frozen computations, so rebuilds are fast.</p>
<p>Next: actually keep this diary up to date.</p>


